Kind: ablation
Issue: #752
Takes out: the privilege check in kernel_task_create() -- both the x86-64 refusal and the i386 host_priv gate -- so a kernel-loaded task is made for any caller, as before #752.  act_test [15], handed KERN_SUCCESS where it required a refusal, makes a thread in that task; on x86-64 the thread reaches pcb_user_to_kernel() and the machine stops (#453), which is the stop the fix prevents.
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 1
Expect: pcb_user_to_kernel: this machine has no kernel-loaded tasks
Expect: making a thread in it to show the cost
diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/task.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/task.c
index 3bcc7884..60bf77f9 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/task.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/task.c
@@ -512,37 +512,12 @@ kernel_task_create(
 	vm_size_t		map_size,
 	task_t			*child_task)
 {
-#ifdef	__x86_64__
-	/*
-	 * x86-64 has no collocation and no kernel-loaded tasks (#453): a thread
-	 * created in a kernel-loaded task panics in pcb_user_to_kernel().  Refuse
-	 * to create one at all, so that neither syscall_kernel_task_create() nor
-	 * the mach.defs kernel_task_create RPC can reach that panic -- from ring 3
-	 * or from anywhere else (#752).  The panic stays the last-resort guard it
-	 * was: this removes the path to it, not the guard.
-	 */
-	(void) parent_task;
-	(void) host;
-	(void) map_base;
-	(void) map_size;
-	(void) child_task;
-	return KERN_NOT_SUPPORTED;
-#else	/* __x86_64__ */
 	kern_return_t		retval;
 	task_t			new_task;
 	task_user_data_data_t	user_data;
 	vm_map_t		old_map;
 
-	/*
-	 * #752: the privileged host port is the authority for making a task in
-	 * the kernel's address space.  Without it, refuse.  The trap resolves it
-	 * with port_name_to_host_priv() and the mach.defs RPC with
-	 * convert_port_to_host_priv(), so both paths are gated the same way, and
-	 * only the holders of host_priv_self (bootstrap and the servers it seeds)
-	 * pass.  x86-64 refuses above, having no kernel-loaded task at all (#453).
-	 */
-	if (host == HOST_NULL)
-		return KERN_NO_ACCESS;
+	(void) host;	/* #752 ablation: the x86-64 refusal and host gate removed */
 
 	/*
 	 * Create the task.
@@ -615,7 +590,6 @@ kernel_task_create(
 #endif	/* MACH_KDB */
 
 	return (KERN_SUCCESS);
-#endif	/* __x86_64__ */
 }
 
 kern_return_t
